{"id":"tiletamine","name":"Tiletamine","form":"capsule","status":"Documented","aliases":"telazol","category":"Dissociative","summarySources":"TripSit","summary":"A relatively rare dissociative anesthetic. The drug is pharmacologically classified as an NMDA receptor antagonist. It is related to other anesthetics in this family such as ketamine and phencyclidine (PCP). The drug has been used to cut ketamine, in which case it may cause additional nausea. In veterinary practice it is mixed with zolazolam which is a potent anaesthetic, at a 1:1 ratio. ","doseMaxTick":150,"doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Oral","bioavailability":"TripSit reference","source":"TripSit","unit":"mg","light":"10–25 mg","common":"25–50 mg","strong":"50–100 mg+","heavy":"100 mg+","commonEstimate":38,"band":{"low":25,"high":50},"domain":[8,135],"segments":{"light":[10,25],"common":[25,50],"strong":[50,100],"heavy":[100,129.6]}},{"roa":"Intramuscular","bioavailability":"TripSit reference","source":"TripSit","unit":"mg","light":"2.5–5 mg","common":"5–10 mg","strong":"10–20 mg+","heavy":"20 mg+","commonEstimate":8,"band":{"low":5,"high":10},"domain":[2,27],"segments":{"light":[2.5,5],"common":[5,10],"strong":[10,20],"heavy":[20,25.92]}}],"durationSources":"TripSit","durationRows":[{"roa":"Oral","onset":"15–45 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–72 h","total":"6–12 h"},{"roa":"Insufflated","onset":"2–10 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–72 h","total":"2–5 h"},{"roa":"Intramuscular","onset":"1–5 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–72 h","total":"1–4 h"},{"roa":"General","onset":"—","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–72 h","total":"—"}],"subjectiveEffects":[],"combinations":[],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/tiletamine"}]}